      "writtenOn": "2017-12-20T03:30:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This highly obscures the function of the code.\nInstead of breaking the common beginning and ending of the code into separate functions, you can do something similar to what overlayfs does, and call into a common function from create and mkdir, and split back into the two function calls on S_ISREG(dentry)/S_ISDIR(dentry). That would remove the need for the functions in create.c, and the structs that they pass.",
